{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["The sense of <b>What is this you have done</b> is: to transgress My commandment. For the woman was included in the warning given to Adam, since she was a bone from his bones at that time, and likewise she is included in his punishment. And He did not say to the woman, 'you have eaten from the tree,' because she was punished for her eating and for her counsel, just as the serpent was punished, and therefore she said, 'the serpent deceived me and I ate,' for the great punishment was on account of the eating. And from this we can derive punishment for one who causes another to sin through speech, as our Rabbis taught us (Pesachim 22b) from the verse, 'and before the blind you shall not place a stumbling block' (Leviticus 19:14)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The Talmudic citation reads פסחים כ\"ב ע\"ז ו, which in standard reference form is Pesachim 22b; the ע\"ז appears to reflect a page/column marker in the manuscript's citation convention and has been rendered as the standard daf reference."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:24:16.489982498Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}